Bins

  - divide each trials neural response into distinct time windows (early middle late) instead of averaging neural activity
    across the entire stimulus. 
  - with 250 neurons and 3 bins you get 750 features per trial


Monet2/Trippy
  - clip analysis has 384 trials across 3 categories (128 each) giving data for 5 fold cross validation after balancing you 
    have 40 samples for 3 classes = 120 trials. 
  - monet2 and trippy each only have 40 trials in a file, if i used the same neuron selection approach, not many neurons will 
    be selected. When you try to 5 fold each fold needs at least 2 samples per class in the test set. leaving with 8 samples per fold
    which is not enough for reliable trianing especially with 6000+ features
  - If I class balance only to take 40 neurons from each class (200 total trials) but with 6000 plus feautres it creates overfitting

